:00-04:56', 'title': 'Nike Inc Reports Fiscal 2021 First Quarter Results', 'text': 'NIKE, INC. REPORTS FISCAL 2021 FIRST QUARTER RESULTS.Q1 EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.95.Q1 REVENUE $10.6 BILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $9.14 BILLION.Q1 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $0.47 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.QTRLY NIKE BRAND DIGITAL SALES INCREASED 82 PERCENT, OR 83 PERCENT ON A CURRENCY-NEUTRAL BASIS.Q1 REVENUE IMPACTED BY STRONG NIKE BRAND DIGITAL GROWTH OF 82 PERCENT, OFFSET BY LOWER REVENUE IN OUR WHOLESALE BUSINESS AND NIKE-OWNED STORES.QUARTER END INVENTORY ROSE 15 PERCENT VERSUS PRIOR YEAR BUT DECREASED 9 PERCENT VERSUS PRIOR QUARTER.CONTINUE TO EXPERIENCE YEAR-OVER-YEAR DECLINES IN PHYSICAL RETAIL TRAFFIC ACROSS MARKETPLACE DUE TO COVID-19 IMPACTS.QTRLY NIKE DIRECT SALES WERE $3.7 BILLION, UP 12 PERCENT ON A REPORTED BASIS.QTRLY REVENUES FOR NIKE BRAND WERE $10.0 BILLION, FLAT TO PRIOR YEAR ON A CURRENCY-NEUTRAL BASIS.QTRLY GREATER CHINA TOTAL REVENUE WAS $1,780 MILLION VERSUS $1,679 MILLION.QTRLY GROSS MARGIN DECREASED 90 BASIS POINTS TO 44.8 PERCENT PRIMARILY AS A RESULT OF IMPACTS FROM COVID-19.QTRLY SELLING AND ADMINISTRATIVE EXPENSE DECREASED 11 PERCENT TO $3.0 BILLION.QTRLY ASIA PACIFIC & LATIN AMERICA REVENUE $1,099 MILLION VERSUS $1,345 MILLION.QTRLY NORTH AMERICA TOTAL REVENUE $4,225  MILLION VERSUS $4,293 MILLION REPORTED LAST YEAR.TOTAL LIQUIDITY AT AUGUST 31 WAS $13.4 BILLION.QTRLY EUROPE, MIDDLE EAST & AFRICA TOTAL REVENUE $2,910  MILLION VERSUS $2,773 MILLION REPORTED LAST YEAR.'}{'symbol': 'NVDA', 'date': '2020-09-23 07:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Li Auto Announces Three-Way Strategic Cooperation With Nvidia', 'text': 'LI AUTO - ANNOUNCED A THREE-WAY STRATEGIC COOPERATION WITH NVIDIA CORPORATION.'}{'symbol': 'PFE', 'date': '2020-09-23 09:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'FDA Accepts Supplemental New Drug Application For Pfizer’S Xalkori For The Treatment Of Pediatric Alk-Positive Anaplastic Large Cell Lymphoma', 'text': 'FDA ACCEPTS SUPPLEMENTAL NEW DRUG APPLICATION FO